PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — ProjectZSlice seal depth reads millimetres as
a layer count (ledger row U2; PicoPie Fix 3 reached the same diagnosis
independently).

Both end-cap seal loops use `(int)(0.5f + m_roGrid->background())` as a
number of z-layers, but background() is the narrow-band half-width in WORLD
units (mm). At 1.0 mm voxels the value coincides with the band (3); above
1.0 mm it over-seals harmlessly (beyond-band layers average to background and
prune away); below 1.0 mm it under-seals — 2 of 3 layers at 0.5-0.7 mm, and
ZERO below ~0.167 mm, leaving projected end caps open. The fix converts to
voxel units with the class's own fToVoxels — the same formula, units fixed.

Verification shape (picovoxel SKv2-0 V0.9): per-scale seal oracles at
{1.5, 1.0, 0.5, 0.167} mm; at 1.0 mm the fixed path is value-identical to the
original (proven at production scale: an unrelated HeatX 1.0 mm content pin
held byte-for-byte across the change).

PROPOSAL, NOT APPLIED LOCALLY: picovoxel ships the fix in a sibling-TU export
(Voxels_ProjectZSliceFast) so the vendored tree stays pristine and the
original remains the differential oracle.

